@startuml sequence-digitalizer-full-run
!include elvira.iuml
' =============================================================================
' What: a full run is choreography around the orchestrator's job ledger: it
'       sends each job with send_task(link=job_done, link_error=job_failed);
'       the worker writes its output and then its outcome file, and Celery
'       itself sends the callback to the orchestrator's queue, which reads the
'       file and sends the next stage. The stage order stays today's (clean →
'       analyze → formulas → render → gate); publication is optional.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, one scenario (a book that passes the gate in a
'       project with a catalog target), proposal. The standalone tasks of
'       ocr-, analyzer-, equation- and render-service share one lifeline: they
'       follow the clean loop exactly. Omitted: telemetry, SSE detail.
' Source: evilflowers-worker runtime.py, outcome.py, settings.py,
'         docs/architecture.md §2-§3.4 @ 8fc9c20; Celery 5.7 docs canvas.html
'         and calling.html (link applied with the return value, single-argument
'         errback for send_task, chords need a result backend); knowledge note
'         Extraction-Pipeline (2026-11-14); this repo
'         studio/workers/stages/orchestrate.py (STAGES), gate.py,
'         docs/design/studio-spec.md (2026-11-16).
' =============================================================================

title Full run of one book: commands out, link callbacks and outcome files back\n(proposal, 2026-11-16)

actor "Operator" as op
participant "Portal\nAPI" as api
participant "Orchestrator\n(job ledger)" as orch <<focus>>
queue "Redis\ndb 8" as redis
participant "scan-\nservice" as scan
participant "ocr · analyzer ·\nequation · render" as more
participant "Catalog\n(dev)" as cat

op -> api : POST runs {kind: full}
api -> orch : Run(queued)
orch -> orch : plan leaves, clean jobs\n(leaf batches), token per job

loop each batch (KEDA scales on queue depth)
  orch -[$accent_msg()]> redis : <b>send_task …scan.clean</b>\n<b>run_id · job · inputs</b>\n<b>outcome · token</b>\n<b>link=job_done</b>\n<b>link_error=job_failed</b>
  redis -> scan : deliver (acks_late)
  scan -> scan : leaves, previews, DZI under\njobs/<job>/; outcome file **last**
  scan -> redis : link: job_done(summary)\n→ digitalizer.portal
  redis -[$accent_msg()]> orch : <b>job_done: read outcome,</b>\n<b>check token, promote</b>
end
orch -> api : run.progress (SSE)

par analyze, same loop as clean
  orch -> redis : …ocr_worker.standalone.hocr ×N
  redis -> more : deliver
  more -> redis : link: job_done
else
  orch -> redis : …analyzer.standalone.layout ×N
  redis -> more : deliver
  more -> redis : link: job_done
end
redis -> orch : job_done ×N (ledger counts)

orch -> redis : …equation.standalone.formulas
redis -> more : deliver
more -> more : formula crops →\nvlm (PaddleOCR-VL)
more -> redis : link: job_done
redis -> orch : job_done

orch -> redis : evilflowers_render.book
redis -> more : deliver
more -> more : MRC PDF · PDF/A-2b ·\nEPUB · IA files, outcome
more -> redis : link: job_done
redis -> orch : job_done: artifacts

orch -> orch : quality gate → approved\n(flagged → review: page\nre-run sequence)

opt the project has a catalog target
  orch -> cat : POST entry +\nacquisitions /api/v1
  cat --> orch : 201 entry id
  cat -> cat : its own extraction run\n(analyzer → text ·\nimage · equation)
end
orch -> api : book.approved / published (SSE)

note over orch, redis
**On failure** the worker raises; Celery sends
job_failed(task_id). **Reconcile** (beat, every
minute) per job past its deadline: an outcome
file without a callback is applied; with no file
the job is re-sent with a new token, and the run
fails once the job's budget is spent.
end note

caption No result backend and no event listener: the callback is an ordinary message on the orchestrator's queue. Workers\nnever call the portal or the catalog. Publication is optional; when it happens, the catalog's own pipeline starts on its own.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-books-digitalizer · docs/diagrams/sequence-digitalizer-full-run.puml
@enduml
